pupil-name-scrubber (the Python package hush, version 0.1.0) includes data derived
from two sources.

1. Office for National Statistics, "Baby names in England and Wales: 1996 to 2025",
   Tables 1 and 2. Contains public sector information licensed
   under the Open Government Licence v3.0:
   https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/
   Used for hush/lists/first_names.txt, name_words.txt, common_first_names.txt and
   name_sex.txt (names given to 10 or more babies over the years; the sex split by a
   four-to-one rule). Source file sha256:
   bf7b10486ab20d0b32e4bc87385112f4555210f61e34eaac3574a0d8a658c0d4

2. SCOWL (Spell Checker Oriented Word Lists), as packaged in Debian and Ubuntu as
   wbritish 2020.12.07. Used for hush/lists/words.txt and to split names from name-words.
   Copyright 2000-2011 by Kevin Atkinson and the other copyright holders named in
   licences/SCOWL-copyright.txt, which carries the full permission notice.

Rebuild both with tools/build_names.py.
